# What does not belong in a distributed plugin.
#
# Note this is applied by rsync while staging, before `composer install --no-dev` runs in the
# stage — so `composer.json` and `composer.lock` are copied in separately by bin/build-zip.sh and
# removed again afterwards. They are needed to build and unwanted in the result.

# Directories
bin
dist
docs
.git
.github
.husky
.wporg
node_modules
src
tests
.idea
.vscode
playwright.config.mjs
test-results
playwright-report
assets/styles

# Development configuration
.distignore
.editorconfig
.eslintrc
.gitignore
.huskyrc.json
.wp-env.json
phpcs.xml
phpunit.xml
phpunit.xml.dist
.phpunit.result.cache
.prettierrc
tailwind.config.js
webpack.config.js
/languages/nfd-site-migrator.php

# `assets/fonts` is deliberately *not* excluded even though webpack emits hashed copies of the
# woff2 files into `build/fonts`. The OFL licence texts live beside the sources, and a font that
# ships without its licence is a licence violation. The duplicated 98KB is the cost of that.

# Working documents. Not `*.md` as a blanket rule: CREDITS.md is the attribution record the GPL
# asks be preserved, and it has to travel with the code it describes. LICENSE has no extension
# and is likewise deliberately absent from this list.
CLAUDE.md
README.md

# File types
*.json
*.lock
*.log
*.sql
*.tar.gz
*.xml
*.yml
*.zip
*.dist
